  "title": "The hidden cost of skipping testing in your marketing campaigns",
  "summary": "Most campaigns skip message and creative testing because it’s seen as slow, expensive, or “nice to have.” But the real price tag shows up later, in wasted spend, rushed rework, and underperforming results. Testing isn’t a line item to cut; it’s the cheapest insurance you’ll ever buy. Skip it, and you’re buying a first-class ticket to the smoking crater of campaign failure.",
